  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/3BDB0B">Definition <span data-tag="3BDB0B">6.1.6.1</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-category which admits pullbacks, and $S$ a collection of morphisms of $\calX $ which is stable under pullback. We will say that a morphism $f: X \rightarrow Y$ <em>classifies $S$</em> if it is a final object of $\calO _{\calX }^{(S)}$ (see Notation <a href="/tag/3F328E" data-tag="3F328E">6.1.3.4</a>). In this situation, we will also say that the object $Y \in \calX $ <em>classifies $S$</em>classifying map!for a collection of morphisms. A <em>subobject classifier</em> for $\calX $ is an object which classifies the collection of all monomorphisms in $\calX $. </p>
